<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-019-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) Ch. VII — tissue cells as hexagons / froth vs. human corneal endothelium (Pass 2: segmented specimen, sweep, controls, statistics) — Code-to-model traceability: 80/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Module docstring maps C1-C3 and steps 1-7 to Thompson pages and equations E1-E6; every function docstring names its law; math_kg code_locus/lean_locus pass the integrity and formula-alignment gates; Fig. 125 crop boxes carry their derivation comment. Segmentation hyper-parameters (blueness 40, min contact 4 px, min_distance) are documented but not derived from the image." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-019-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-019-code-traceability-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-019-code-traceability-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-019-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) Ch. VII — tissue cells as hexagons / froth vs. human corneal endothelium (Pass 2: segmented specimen, sweep, controls, statistics) — Model fidelity to source: 78/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The froth laws (E1-E5) are implemented exactly and proved in Lean; the claim is now actually tested — Euler mean six, trivalency, honeycomb bound and hexagon fraction are all measured on tissue and on Thompson's own Fig. 125. The division chain (E6) reproduces Gibson's spectrum to 0.03 and its ablation shows cleavage geometry matters. Remaining gap: least perimeter is modelled by Lloyd relaxation (a proxy), and the froth model class cannot match topology and area dispersion simultaneously (joint fit), which the script records rather than hides." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "thompson/claims/t1917-019_the-forms-of-tissues-or-cell-aggregates.py L151–L163: lloyd_step remains a centroidal-Voronoi proxy for surface-tension relaxation <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/f1b27eb65/thompson/claims/t1917-019_the-forms-of-tissues-or-cell-aggregates.py#L151-L163>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-019-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-019-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-019-model-fidelity-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-019-model-fidelity-4> ;
    pk:hasScore 7.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-019-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) Ch. VII — tissue cells as hexagons / froth vs. human corneal endothelium (Pass 2: segmented specimen, sweep, controls, statistics) — Morphometric validation: 74/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "16 measurements, 14 measured on the specimen or the 1917 plate, each with a literature reference: p6 0.659 vs clinical norm 0.616 (within 0.55-0.70), area CV 0.285 vs 0.315, <n> 5.89 vs 6, trivalent 1.00 vs 1, Lewis lambda 0.18 vs 0.25, Aboav a 0.74 vs 1.2, excess perimeter 8.6 % vs the Hales bound 0; bootstrap 95 % CIs; r / RMSE / TV / KS and chi-square against Gibson, best froth, honeycomb and Poisson null; pipeline control quantifies pixel-perimeter and finite-window bias. Limits: n = 1, no um scale, and the measured excess perimeter conflates polygon irregularity with wall waviness." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "thompson/claims/t1917-019_the-forms-of-tissues-or-cell-aggregates.py L721–L731: analyse_specimen: single image, pixel units only <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/f1b27eb65/thompson/claims/t1917-019_the-forms-of-tissues-or-cell-aggregates.py#L721-L731>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-019-measurement-division-topology-chain-fixed-point-p6-through-centre-cleavage-reconstruction>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-019-measurement-pearson-r-specimen-vs-best-fit-froth-model-polygon-distribution>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-019-measurement-pearson-r-specimen-vs-gibson-2006-polygon-distribution-n-4-8>,
