<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-019-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) Ch. VII — tissue cells as hexagons / froth vs. human corneal endothelium (Pass 2: segmented specimen, sweep, controls, statistics) — MorphoEval overall 77.5/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Specimen (85 interior cells of 126): <n> = 5.894 [95 % CI 5.78, 6.01], window-bias corrected 6.08; p6 = 0.659 [0.55, 0.77], p5 = 0.224, p7 = 0.118, mu2 = 0.34; 100 % trivalent junctions; median shape index 3.96 (regular hexagon 3.72, square 4.00); area CV 0.285 vs clinical norm 0.315; excess perimeter 7.7 % raw, 8.6 % after the rasterised-froth pipeline correction; Lewis lambda 0.18 (Lewis 1928: 0.25); Aboav a = 0.74 (froths 1.0-1.5), neighbour-shuffle control a = 6.1. Thompson's Fig. 125: A (compressed) p6 = 0.89, B (relaxed) p6 = 0.97. Best topology fit: fully relaxed CVT froth (delta = 1.0, Lloyd = 20), TV = 0.054, r = 0.99, chi-square p = 0.42; joint topology+geometry fit (delta = 0.2, Lloyd = 0) cannot match the tissue's area CV (model 0.18) — the froth model class reproduces the tissue's topology but not its size dispersion. Specimen vs Gibson 2006 proliferating spectrum: r = 0.94, RMSE 0.10, chi-square p = 0.005 (significantly more hexagonal). Verdict: SUPPORTED on Thompson's own exemplar tissue (C1 mean six, C2 least perimeter within 10 %, C3 p6 modal and >= 0.5), qualified for proliferating epithelia. Overall 77.5/100 (faithfulness 75.3, reproducibility 82.7); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit f1b27eb65; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 78, Morphological realism / specimen match 72, Parameter expressivity 80, Morphometric validation 74, Source and data traceability 88, Code-to-model traceability 80, Reproducibility package 80. Output judged: docs/media/t1917_019_the_forms_of_tissues_or_cell_a_comparison.png: rendered output of thompson/claims/t1917-019_the-forms-of-tissues-or-cell-aggregates.py at f1b27eb65, image/png, 783069 B, 1600×1300 px, artifact_sha256 12cce483342dadf13115a47e56930376f60359a117a1a04c62c1fd0f1105b924 (sha256 12cce483342dadf13115a47e56930376f60359a117a1a04c62c1fd0f1105b924), spec_fingerprint 573eaa78956bb7a95427321ba84764635768abd58c2fd7fd76e7660dc905fc59. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 573eaa78956bb7a95427321ba84764635768abd58c2fd7fd76e7660dc905fc59; artifact_sha256: 12cce483342dadf13115a47e56930376f60359a117a1a04c62c1fd0f1105b924; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-019/elodea_canadensis_leaf_specimen.jpg=ffa66c5d5bfa1afb..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-019/human_corneal_endothelium_specimen.jpg=9daed5fb546e11bf..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-019/thompson_1917_p322_fig125_126_froth_elodea.jpg=1a31755fe8c43ca4...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-28-t1917-019-the-forms-of-tissues-or-cell-a-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Thompson p. 305: cellular tissue resembles a froth | Thompson p. 309/323: partitions meet three at a point at ~120 degrees (Lamarle minimal-area condition) | Thompson p. 321: hexagonal pattern illustrated in countless cases but perfectly regular only rarely; eye pigment epithelium as the exemplar | Thompson p. 325: cells on the average hexagonal, some with fewer and some with more sides than six | Thompson p. 330: closely packed hexagons give the minimal extent of boundary in a plane | Thompson Fig. 125 (after Rhumbler): soap froth between plates, compressed (A) and relaxed (B); reconstructed_in_script: Periodic Voronoi froth morphospace with Gaussian positional disorder delta and Lloyd relaxation; Poisson-Voronoi null | Nucleus-marker watershed segmentation of the alizarin-red corneal endothelium; distance-peak watershed for line drawings | Interior-cell polygon statistics, Crofton perimeters, 2x2-window junction valence, Lewis and Aboav-Weaire fits, bootstrap CIs | Mean-field Gibson 2006 division-topology Markov chain with through-centre cleavage (reconstruction; uniform-random cleavage ablation) | Rasterised-froth pipeline control: pixel perimeter bias (-0.9 %) and finite-window <n> bias (-0.18) measured on a tessellation with known exact statistics; transfer_boundary: Lloyd (centroidal Voronoi) relaxation is a proxy for surface-tension perimeter minimisation, not a Plateau / vertex-model energy descent | The honeycomb bound is applied cell-by-cell to the measured area distribution (Hales 2001 proves the equal-area case); the measured excess includes real wall waviness as well as polygon irregularity | Clinical norms (Sheng & Bullimore 2007) are specular-microscopy regressions for living corneas; the specimen is an ex vivo alizarin-red flat mount; does_not_claim: n = 1 specimen: no population statement about human corneal endothelia | No um/px scale, so no cell density or absolute area is reported | The proliferating-epithelium qualification rests on Gibson 2006's published spectrum, not on a segmented proliferating specimen | The Elodea canadensis image (Thompson Fig. 126 species) is vendored for visual comparison only; chloroplast clutter defeats the automatic pipeline." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "open need [independent_assessor/model-fidelity, pressure P=0.5]: Cross-provider second assessor",
        "open need [specimen_comparison/morphometric-validation, pressure P=4.0]: Segmented proliferating epithelium to test the Gibson 2006 regime on data rather than from the literature spectrum",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R10', 'item': 'Replace Lloyd relaxation by a Plateau / vertex-model energy descent (Farhadifar 2007) so that least perimeter is minimised, not proxied'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R11', 'item': 'Separate wall waviness from polygon irregularity in the excess perimeter (vertex-to-vertex polygonal perimeter vs Crofton perimeter)'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R7', 'item': 'Independent cross-provider second assessor — still builder-scored'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R8', 'item': 'More specimens: >= 5 corneal endothelia and at least one segmented proliferating epithelium (e.g. Drosophila wing disc) to test the Gibson regime directly rather than from the published spectrum'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R9', 'item': 'Attach a um/px scale (specular-microscopy field or scale-bar specimen) to report cell density and absolute areas'}" ;
    pk:hasScore 7.75e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

